  "changes": [
    "Added automatic RC4 code-asset recovery using strings referenced by DEX const-string instructions. Unused string-pool entries cannot supply a key.",
    "Recovery is independent of family names, asset filenames and the historical key. It supports direct classic DEX and ZIP containers with renamed DEX members.",
    "Require complete DEX SHA-1/Adler-32 checks, or bounded ZIP member size/CRC checks plus a validated DEX. Recovered code enters the ordinary recursive scanner; RC4-encrypted executable code is suspicious code concealment, without implying a hostile payload.",
    "Added source-asset and key-literal offset provenance without exposing the key. Marked the archive-member encoding observation suspicious when executable code is successfully recovered; ordinary RC4 data processing is outside this matcher.",
    "Tightened authenticator evidence to a 512-byte cluster and required text reads within 512 bytes of each wallet query. Kept descriptions limited to targeting, text reads and PIN/OTP records rather than asserting a proven source-to-network transfer.",
    "Removed android-accessibility-sms-banker-control: SMS permission declarations, accessibility references and BOOT_COMPLETED references do not establish hostile remote control or installed persistence.",
    "Moved four Android API class-descriptor facts from behavioral/privilege homes to metadata/binary/symbols/descriptor. Matchers and effective scopes are preserved, and all direct consumers are remapped.",
    "Renamed the accessibility service-config union to android-accessibility-surface-references; an API descriptor alone does not establish a configured service.",
    "Added a neutral referenced-literal observation for hyphen-separated 106-series number constants. The SMS recipient is unresolved at the branch join, so the finding does not claim a bound destination or premium billing. Clarified BOOT_COMPLETED-string and encoded-private-header descriptions."
  ],
